s>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Jass</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Houlston</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Atkin</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>Tomlinson</surname><given-names>IP</given-names></name><name><surname>Silver</surname><given-names>AR</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Exon 3 beta-catenin mutations are specifically associated with colorectal carcinomas in the hereditary non-polyposis colorectal cancer syndrome</article-title><source>Gut</source><year>2005b</year><volume>54</volume><fpage>264</fpage><lpage>267</lpage>doi:10.1136/gut.2004.048132<!--PubMed citation query: 'Gut||54|264||bib5|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15647192</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib6"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lagerstedt Robinson</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Liu</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Vandrovcova</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Halvarsson</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Clendenning</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Frebourg</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Papadopoulos</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Kinzler</surname><given-names>KW</given-names></name><name><surname>Vogelstein</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Peltomaki</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Kolodner</surname><given-names>RD</given-names></name><name><surname>Nilbert</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Lindbolm</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Lynch syndrome (hereditary nonpolyposis colorectal cancer) diagnostics</article-title><source>J Natl Cancer Inst</source><year>2007</year><volume>99</volume><fpage>291</fpage><lpage>299</lpage><!--